Relative odds and the history of getting to level 5.  The odds of
getting Excalibur are 1-in-6 per dip.  The odds of the fountain
disappearing if you don't get Excalibur are 1-in-3 per dip.  That
means that you can easily go through several fountains disappearing
before you get one that gives you Excalibur and disappears.  If
you are likely to go through several, may as well start at the one
closest to the exit because later in the game you'll spend more and
more time deeper and you never know when you'll want a fountain on
some random level.

Combine this with the fact that getting to level 5 probably happened
before you completed mines+sokoban so you haven't explored much of
the dungeon yet.  Going to known places in the attempt to get
Excalibur makes more sense than exploring deeper for the purpose.

Also there's the fact that using the minetown fountains is certain
to make them disappear on the second use each, and having them
disappear is certain to anger the guards.  So it's best to start
trying elsewhere.  Unless your pets already took out the guards
or you decided to act unlike a lawfull and you did it yourself.

